From: MFEC AI Lab <wason@mfec.co.th>
Subject: [PATCH] qwen35: apply the Hadamard inverse to the MTP embedding lookup

The MTP draft graph builds its own token-embedding lookup instead of going
through llm_graph_context::build_inp_embd(). On a model that declares
prism.hadamard.inverse_weight_names (PrismML ternary Bonsai), token_embd.weight
is stored in the latent/rotated domain, and every read of it must restore the
primal basis immediately after the lookup.

Without this, llama_verify_hadamard_graph rejects context creation:

    llama_verify_hadamard_graph: latent lookup 'mtp_tok_embd-64' consumed by
        op=RMS_NORM name='norm-64' src0 hint=0
    llama_init_from_model: failed to initialize the context:
        Hadamard-latent table 'token_embd.weight' is read without the inverse transform

This mirrors the main path in llama-graph.cpp (build_inp_embd), including its
operation order: for the inverse transform the rotation is applied first and the
sign flip second, which is the reverse of the forward/folded path in
build_lora_mm.

The MTP shared head needs no change: it goes through build_lora_mm(), which
already applies hadamard_rotations to the activation before the matmul.

--- a/src/models/qwen35.cpp
+++ b/src/models/qwen35.cpp
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #include "models.h"
 #include "llama-memory-recurrent.h"
+#include "llama-impl.h"   // llama_mul_mat_hadamard
 
@@ -594,6 +595,20 @@
     if (ubatch.token) {
         ggml_tensor * tok_embd_w = layer.nextn.embed_tokens ? layer.nextn.embed_tokens : model.tok_embd;
 
         tok_embd = ggml_get_rows(ctx0, tok_embd_w, inp->tokens);
+
+        // A Hadamard-latent embedding table stores rotated rows; restore the
+        // primal basis right after the lookup: h = s * (H z). The main graph
+        // does this in llm_graph_context::build_inp_embd(); the MTP graph has
+        // its own lookup and must do the same or llama_verify_hadamard_graph
+        // rejects the context.
+        if (hadamard_inverses) {
+            const auto it = hadamard_inverses->find(tok_embd_w);
+            if (it != hadamard_inverses->end()) {
+                tok_embd = llama_mul_mat_hadamard(ctx0, tok_embd, it->second.rot);
+                if (it->second.signs) {
+                    tok_embd = ggml_mul(ctx0, tok_embd, it->second.signs);
+                }
+            }
+        }
     } else {
         tok_embd = inp->embd;
     }
